.77\", \"version_raw\": \"000000103000000000000126400000077\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Heap buffer overflow in libwebp in Google Chrome prior to 116.0.5845.187 and libwebp 1.3.2 allowed a remote attacker to perform an out of bounds memory write via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Critical)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4863\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-787\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Sun, 07 Jan 2024 11:15:13 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 12 Sep 2023 15:15:24 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"edge\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft\", \"software_version\": \"103.0.1264.77\", \"version_raw\": \"000000103000000000000126400000077\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent token handler versions 3.2.6 and below, suffer from a Directory Traversal vulnerability whereby unsanitized input from a CLI argument flows into io.ioutil.WriteFile, where it is used as a path. This can result in a Path Traversal vulnerability and allow an attacker to write arbitrary files. This issue is remediated in version 3.3.0 via safe guards that reject inputs that attempt to do path traversal.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-2273\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.5\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.5, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.5\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\", \"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 3.6, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 May 2023 17:52:05 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 26 Apr 2023 09:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7\", \"software_version\": \"3.1.6.44\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000010000000600000044\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent, versions prior to 3.1.3, suffer from an improper access control vulnerability whereby, the user has access to the snapshot directory. An attacker can access, read and copy any of the files in this directory e.g. asset_info.json or file_info.json, leading to a loss of confidentiality. This issue was fixed in Rapid7 Insight Agent 3.1.3.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4016\", \"cve_severity\": \"LOW\", \"cvss\": 3.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"2.1\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 2.1, \"cvss3_score\": \"3.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 3.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 3.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-Other\", \"CWE-284\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Fri, 05 Aug 2022 11:09:58 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 21 Jan 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000000000000400000001\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent, versions 3.0.1 to 3.1.2.34, suffer from a local privilege escalation due to an uncontrolled DLL search path. Specifically, when Insight Agent versions 3.0.1 to 3.1.2.34 start, the Python interpreter attempts to load python3.dll at \\\"C:\\\\DLLs\\\\python3.dll,\\\" which normally is writable by locally authenticated users. Because of this, a malicious local user could use Insight Agent\u0027s startup conditions to elevate to SYSTEM privileges. This issue was fixed in Rapid7 Insight Agent 3.1.2.35. This vulnerability is a regression of CVE-2019-5629.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4007\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"7.2\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 7.2, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-427\", \"CWE-427\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 21 Dec 2021 14:52:22 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 14 Dec 2021 15:15:07 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000000000000400000001\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent versions 3.1.2.38 and earlier suffer from a privilege escalation vulnerability, whereby an attacker can hijack the flow of execution due to an unquoted argument to the runas.exe command used by the ir_agent.exe component, resulting in elevated rights and persistent access to the machine. This issue was fixed in Rapid7 Insight Agent version 3.1.3.80.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-0237\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"7.2\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 7.2, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-428\", \"CWE-264\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 24 Mar 2022 19:21:21 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Thu, 17 Mar 2022 23:15:07 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000000000000400000001\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent token handler versions 3.2.6 and below, suffer from a Directory Traversal vulnerability whereby unsanitized input from a CLI argument flows into io.ioutil.WriteFile, where it is used as a path. This can result in a Path Traversal vulnerability and allow an attacker to write arbitrary files. This issue is remediated in version 3.3.0 via safe guards that reject inputs that attempt to do path traversal.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-2273\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.5\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.5, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.5\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\", \"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 3.6, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 May 2023 17:52:05 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 26 Apr 2023 09:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000000000000400000001\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Heap buffer overflow in GPU in Google Chrome prior to 107.0.5304.121 allowed a remote attacker who had compromised the renderer process to potentially perform a sandbox escape via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: High)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-4135\", \"cve_severity\": \"CRITICAL\", \"cvss\": 9.6, \"cvss3_score\": \"9.6\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 9.6, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 9.6\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-787\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 6.0, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 15 Feb 2024 02:00:01 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 25 Nov 2022 01:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"edge\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft\", \"software_version\": \"103.0.1264.77\", \"version_raw\": \"000000103000000000000126400000077\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Heap buffer overflow in libwebp in Google Chrome prior to 116.0.5845.187 and libwebp 1.3.2 allowed a remote attacker to perform an out of bounds memory write via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Critical)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4863\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-787\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Sun, 07 Jan 2024 11:15:13 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 12 Sep 2023 15:15:24 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"edge\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft\", \"software_version\": \"103.0.1264.77\", \"version_raw\": \"000000103000000000000126400000077\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent token handler versions 3.2.6 and below, suffer from a Directory Traversal vulnerability whereby unsanitized input from a CLI argument flows into io.ioutil.WriteFile, where it is used as a path. This can result in a Path Traversal vulnerability and allow an attacker to write arbitrary files. This issue is remediated in version 3.3.0 via safe guards that reject inputs that attempt to do path traversal.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-2273\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.5\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.5, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.5\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\", \"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 3.6, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 May 2023 17:52:05 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 26 Apr 2023 09:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7\", \"software_version\": \"3.1.5.15\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000010000000500000015\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"A vulnerability in multiple Atlassian products allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to bypass Servlet Filters used by first and third party apps. The impact depends on which filters are used by each app, and how the filters are used. This vulnerability can result in authentication bypass and cross-site scripting. Atlassian has released updates that fix the root cause of this vulnerability, but has not exhaustively enumerated all potential consequences of this vulnerability. Atlassian Bamboo versions are affected before 8.0.9, from 8.1.0 before 8.1.8, and from 8.2.0 before 8.2.4. Atlassian Bitbucket versions are affected before 7.6.16, from 7.7.0 before 7.17.8, from 7.18.0 before 7.19.5, from 7.20.0 before 7.20.2, from 7.21.0 before 7.21.2, and versions 8.0.0 and 8.1.0. Atlassian Confluence versions are affected before 7.4.17, from 7.5.0 before 7.13.7, from 7.14.0 before 7.14.3, from 7.15.0 before 7.15.2, from 7.16.0 before 7.16.4, from 7.17.0 before 7.17.4, and version 7.21.0. Atlassian Crowd versions are affected before 4.3.8, from 4.4.0 before 4.4.2, and version 5.0.0. Atlassian Fisheye and Crucible versions before 4.8.10 are affected. Atlassian Jira versions are affected before 8.13.22, from 8.14.0 before 8.20.10, and from 8.21.0 before 8.22.4. Atlassian Jira Service Management versions are affected before 4.13.22, from 4.14.0 before 4.20.10, and from 4.21.0 before 4.22.4.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26136\", \"cve_severity\": \"CRITICAL\", \"cvss\": 9.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"9.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 9.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 9.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-287\", \"CWE-180\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:50:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 20 Jul 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"The Atlassian Troubleshooting and Support Tools plugin prior to version 1.17.2 allows an unprivileged user to initiate periodic log scans and send the results to a user-specified email address due to a missing authorization check. The email message may contain configuration information about the application that the plugin is installed into. A vulnerable version of the plugin is included with Bitbucket Server / Data Center before 6.6.0, Confluence Server / Data Center before 7.0.1, Jira Server / Data Center before 8.3.2, Crowd / Crowd Data Center before 3.6.0, Fisheye before 4.7.2, Crucible before 4.7.2, and Bamboo before 6.10.2.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-15005\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-862\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 14 Nov 2019 21:15:11 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 08 Nov 2019 04:15:10 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"A vulnerability in multiple Atlassian products allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to cause additional Servlet Filters to be invoked when the application processes requests or responses. Atlassian has confirmed and fixed the only known security issue associated with this vulnerability: Cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) bypass. Sending a specially crafted HTTP request can invoke the Servlet Filter used to respond to CORS requests, resulting in a CORS bypass. An attacker that can trick a user into requesting a malicious URL can access the vulnerable application with the victim\\u2019s permissions. Atlassian Bamboo versions are affected before 8.0.9, from 8.1.0 before 8.1.8, and from 8.2.0 before 8.2.4. Atlassian Bitbucket versions are affected before 7.6.16, from 7.7.0 before 7.17.8, from 7.18.0 before 7.19.5, from 7.20.0 before 7.20.2, from 7.21.0 before 7.21.2, and versions 8.0.0 and 8.1.0. Atlassian Confluence versions are affected before 7.4.17, from 7.5.0 before 7.13.7, from 7.14.0 before 7.14.3, from 7.15.0 before 7.15.2, from 7.16.0 before 7.16.4, from 7.17.0 before 7.17.4, and version 7.21.0. Atlassian Crowd versions are affected before 4.3.8, from 4.4.0 before 4.4.2, and version 5.0.0. Atlassian Fisheye and Crucible versions before 4.8.10 are affected. Atlassian Jira versions are affected before 8.13.22, from 8.14.0 before 8.20.10, and from 8.21.0 before 8.22.4. Atlassian Jira Service Management versions are affected before 4.13.22, from 4.14.0 before 4.20.10, and from 4.21.0 before 4.22.4.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26137\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-346\", \"CWE-180\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:45:16 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 20 Jul 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"The Github repository importer in Atlassian Bitbucket Server before version 5.3.0 allows remote attackers to determine if a service they could not otherwise reach has open ports via a Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18036\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-918\", \"CWE-918\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 09 Oct 2019 23:25:47 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 02 Feb 2018 14:29:00 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Bitbucket Server and Bitbucket Data Center versions starting from 1.0.0 before 5.16.11, from version 6.0.0 before 6.0.11, from version 6.1.0 before 6.1.9, from version 6.2.0 before 6.2.7, from version 6.3.0 before 6.3.6, from version 6.4.0 before 6.4.4, from version 6.5.0 before 6.5.3, from version 6.6.0 before 6.6.3, from version 6.7.0 before 6.7.3, from version 6.8.0 before 6.8.2, from version 6.9.0 before 6.9.1 had a Remote Code Execution vulnerability via the post-receive hook. A remote attacker with permission to clone and push files to a repository on the victim\u0027s Bitbucket Server or Bitbucket Data Center instance, can exploit this vulnerability to execute arbitrary commands on the Bitbucket Server or Bitbucket Data Center systems, using a file with specially crafted content.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-20097\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Mon, 24 Aug 2020 17:37:01 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 15 Jan 2020 21:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Atlassian Bitbucket Server before 4.7.1 allows remote attackers to read the first line of an arbitrary file via a directory traversal attack on the pull requests resource.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2016-4320\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Fri, 12 Oct 2018 18:28:06 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Mon, 10 Apr 2017 03:59:01 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"The repository settings resource in Atlassian Bitbucket Server before version 5.6.0 allows remote attackers to read the first line of arbitrary files via a path traversal vulnerability through the default branch name.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18038\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 5.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"5.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 5.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"5.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 5.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 5.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 14 Feb 2018 14:09:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 02 Feb 2018 14:29:00 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"A vulnerability in multiple Atlassian products allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to bypass Servlet Filters used by first and third party apps. The impact depends on which filters are used by each app, and how the filters are used. This vulnerability can result in authentication bypass and cross-site scripting. Atlassian has released updates that fix the root cause of this vulnerability, but has not exhaustively enumerated all potential consequences of this vulnerability. Atlassian Bamboo versions are affected before 8.0.9, from 8.1.0 before 8.1.8, and from 8.2.0 before 8.2.4. Atlassian Bitbucket versions are affected before 7.6.16, from 7.7.0 before 7.17.8, from 7.18.0 before 7.19.5, from 7.20.0 before 7.20.2, from 7.21.0 before 7.21.2, and versions 8.0.0 and 8.1.0. Atlassian Confluence versions are affected before 7.4.17, from 7.5.0 before 7.13.7, from 7.14.0 before 7.14.3, from 7.15.0 before 7.15.2, from 7.16.0 before 7.16.4, from 7.17.0 before 7.17.4, and version 7.21.0. Atlassian Crowd versions are affected before 4.3.8, from 4.4.0 before 4.4.2, and version 5.0.0. Atlassian Fisheye and Crucible versions before 4.8.10 are affected. Atlassian Jira versions are affected before 8.13.22, from 8.14.0 before 8.20.10, and from 8.21.0 before 8.22.4. Atlassian Jira Service Management versions are affected before 4.13.22, from 4.14.0 before 4.20.10, and from 4.21.0 before 4.22.4.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26136\", \"cve_severity\": \"CRITICAL\", \"cvss\": 9.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"9.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 9.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 9.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-287\", \"CWE-180\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:50:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 20 Jul 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"The Atlassian Troubleshooting and Support Tools plugin prior to version 1.17.2 allows an unprivileged user to initiate periodic log scans and send the results to a user-specified email address due to a missing authorization check. The email message may contain configuration information about the application that the plugin is installed into. A vulnerable version of the plugin is included with Bitbucket Server / Data Center before 6.6.0, Confluence Server / Data Center before 7.0.1, Jira Server / Data Center before 8.3.2, Crowd / Crowd Data Center before 3.6.0, Fisheye before 4.7.2, Crucible before 4.7.2, and Bamboo before 6.10.2.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-15005\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-862\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 14 Nov 2019 21:15:11 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 08 Nov 2019 04:15:10 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"A vulnerability in multiple Atlassian products allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to cause additional Servlet Filters to be invoked when the application processes requests or responses. Atlassian has confirmed and fixed the only known security issue associated with this vulnerability: Cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) bypass. Sending a specially crafted HTTP request can invoke the Servlet Filter used to respond to CORS requests, resulting in a CORS bypass. An attacker that can trick a user into requesting a malicious URL can access the vulnerable application with the victim\\u2019s permissions. Atlassian Bamboo versions are affected before 8.0.9, from 8.1.0 before 8.1.8, and from 8.2.0 before 8.2.4. Atlassian Bitbucket versions are affected before 7.6.16, from 7.7.0 before 7.17.8, from 7.18.0 before 7.19.5, from 7.20.0 before 7.20.2, from 7.21.0 before 7.21.2, and versions 8.0.0 and 8.1.0. Atlassian Confluence versions are affected before 7.4.17, from 7.5.0 before 7.13.7, from 7.14.0 before 7.14.3, from 7.15.0 before 7.15.2, from 7.16.0 before 7.16.4, from 7.17.0 before 7.17.4, and version 7.21.0. Atlassian Crowd versions are affected before 4.3.8, from 4.4.0 before 4.4.2, and version 5.0.0. Atlassian Fisheye and Crucible versions before 4.8.10 are affected. Atlassian Jira versions are affected before 8.13.22, from 8.14.0 before 8.20.10, and from 8.21.0 before 8.22.4. Atlassian Jira Service Management versions are affected before 4.13.22, from 4.14.0 before 4.20.10, and from 4.21.0 before 4.22.4.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26137\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-346\", \"CWE-180\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:45:16 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 20 Jul 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"The Github repository importer in Atlassian Bitbucket Server before version 5.3.0 allows remote attackers to determine if a service they could not otherwise reach has open ports via a Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18036\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-918\", \"CWE-918\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 09 Oct 2019 23:25:47 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 02 Feb 2018 14:29:00 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Bitbucket Server and Bitbucket Data Center versions starting from 1.0.0 before 5.16.11, from version 6.0.0 before 6.0.11, from version 6.1.0 before 6.1.9, from version 6.2.0 before 6.2.7, from version 6.3.0 before 6.3.6, from version 6.4.0 before 6.4.4, from version 6.5.0 before 6.5.3, from version 6.6.0 before 6.6.3, from version 6.7.0 before 6.7.3, from version 6.8.0 before 6.8.2, from version 6.9.0 before 6.9.1 had a Remote Code Execution vulnerability via the post-receive hook. A remote attacker with permission to clone and push files to a repository on the victim\u0027s Bitbucket Server or Bitbucket Data Center instance, can exploit this vulnerability to execute arbitrary commands on the Bitbucket Server or Bitbucket Data Center systems, using a file with specially crafted content.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-20097\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Mon, 24 Aug 2020 17:37:01 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 15 Jan 2020 21:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Atlassian Bitbucket Server before 4.7.1 allows remote attackers to read the first line of an arbitrary file via a directory traversal attack on the pull requests resource.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2016-4320\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Fri, 12 Oct 2018 18:28:06 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Mon, 10 Apr 2017 03:59:01 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"The repository settings resource in Atlassian Bitbucket Server before version 5.6.0 allows remote attackers to read the first line of arbitrary files via a path traversal vulnerability through the default branch name.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18038\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 5.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"5.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 5.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"5.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 5.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 5.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 14 Feb 2018 14:09:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 02 Feb 2018 14:29:00 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent token handler versions 3.2.6 and below, suffer from a Directory Traversal vulnerability whereby unsanitized input from a CLI argument flows into io.ioutil.WriteFile, where it is used as a path. This can result in a Path Traversal vulnerability and allow an attacker to write arbitrary files. This issue is remediated in version 3.3.0 via safe guards that reject inputs that attempt to do path traversal.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-2273\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.5\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.5, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.5\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\", \"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 3.6, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 May 2023 17:52:05 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 26 Apr 2023 09:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, llc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.1.6.44\", \"version_raw\": \"000000003000000010000000600000044\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Use after free in WebXR in Google Chrome prior to 114.0.5735.133 allowed a remote attacker to potentially exploit heap corruption via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: High)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-3217\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-416\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 31 Jan 2024 17:15:12 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 13 Jun 2023 18:15:22 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"google chrome\", \"software_vendor\": \"google inc.\", \"software_version\": \"104.0.5112.88\", \"version_raw\": \"000000104000000000000511200000088\"}, {\"cve_description\": \"Inappropriate implementation in PictureInPicture in Google Chrome prior to 113.0.5672.63 allowed a remote attacker who had compromised the renderer process to obfuscate the security UI via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Low)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-2468\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\