s2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Fri, 12 Oct 2018 18:28:06 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Mon, 10 Apr 2017 03:59:01 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18036\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18036\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.33182, \"epss.score\": 0.00081}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"The Github repository importer in Atlassian Bitbucket Server before version 5.3.0 allows remote attackers to determine if a service they could not otherwise reach has open ports via a Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18036\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-918\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 09 Oct 2019 23:25:47 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 02 Feb 2018 14:29:00 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18038\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18038\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.59793, \"epss.score\": 0.00223}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"The repository settings resource in Atlassian Bitbucket Server before version 5.6.0 allows remote attackers to read the first line of arbitrary files via a path traversal vulnerability through the default branch name.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2017-18038\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 5.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"5.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 5.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"5.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 5.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 5.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-22\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Wed, 14 Feb 2018 14:09:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 02 Feb 2018 14:29:00 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-15005\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-15005\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.20194, \"epss.score\": 0.00054}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"The Atlassian Troubleshooting and Support Tools plugin prior to version 1.17.2 allows an unprivileged user to initiate periodic log scans and send the results to a user-specified email address due to a missing authorization check. The email message may contain configuration information about the application that the plugin is installed into. A vulnerable version of the plugin is included with Bitbucket Server / Data Center before 6.6.0, Confluence Server / Data Center before 7.0.1, Jira Server / Data Center before 8.3.2, Crowd / Crowd Data Center before 3.6.0, Fisheye before 4.7.2, Crucible before 4.7.2, and Bamboo before 6.10.2.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-15005\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-862\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 14 Nov 2019 21:15:11 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 08 Nov 2019 04:15:10 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-20097\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-20097\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.67685, \"epss.score\": 0.0028}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Bitbucket Server and Bitbucket Data Center versions starting from 1.0.0 before 5.16.11, from version 6.0.0 before 6.0.11, from version 6.1.0 before 6.1.9, from version 6.2.0 before 6.2.7, from version 6.3.0 before 6.3.6, from version 6.4.0 before 6.4.4, from version 6.5.0 before 6.5.3, from version 6.6.0 before 6.6.3, from version 6.7.0 before 6.7.3, from version 6.8.0 before 6.8.2, from version 6.9.0 before 6.9.1 had a Remote Code Execution vulnerability via the post-receive hook. A remote attacker with permission to clone and push files to a repository on the victim\u0027s Bitbucket Server or Bitbucket Data Center instance, can exploit this vulnerability to execute arbitrary commands on the Bitbucket Server or Bitbucket Data Center systems, using a file with specially crafted content.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2019-20097\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Mon, 24 Aug 2020 17:37:01 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 15 Jan 2020 21:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-0951\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-0951\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.07513, \"epss.score\": 0.00043}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-0951\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Tue, 08 Sep 2020 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-0951\", \"msrc.title\": \"Windows Defender Application Control Security Feature Bypass Vulnerability\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"\u003cp\u003eA security feature bypass vulnerability exists in Windows Defender Application Control (WDAC) which could allow an attacker to bypass WDAC enforcement. An attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability could execute PowerShell commands that would be blocked by WDAC.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eTo exploit the vulnerability, an attacker need administrator access on a local machine where PowerShell is running. The attacker could then connect to a PowerShell session and send commands to execute arbitrary code.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eThe update addresses the vulnerability by correcting how PowerShell commands are validated when WDAC protection is enabled.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-0951\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 6.7, \"cvss2_score\": \"7.2\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 7.2, \"cvss3_score\": \"6.7\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 6.7, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 6.7\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 0.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Sun, 31 Dec 2023 22:15:48 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 11 Sep 2020 17:15:15 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"powershell\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"7.1.3.sha:.33ce13a0df94183fde13a07ddee0722a017a8d1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10517\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10517\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.25292, \"epss.score\": 0.00063}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"An improper access control vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that allowed authenticated users of the instance to determine the names of unauthorized private repositories given their numerical IDs. This vulnerability did not allow unauthorized access to any repository content besides the name. This vulnerability affected all versions of GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 2.22 and was fixed in versions 2.21.6, 2.20.15, and 2.19.21. This vulnerability was reported via the GitHub Bug Bounty program.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10517\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\", \"CWE-285\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 07 Oct 2021 17:07:22 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Thu, 27 Aug 2020 22:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"github.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"github.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"An improper access control vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that allowed authenticated users of the instance to determine the names of unauthorized private repositories given their numerical IDs. This vulnerability did not allow unauthorized access to any repository content besides the name. This vulnerability affected all versions of GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 2.22 and was fixed in versions 2.21.6, 2.20.15, and 2.19.21. This vulnerability was reported via the GitHub Bug Bounty program.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10517\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.0\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.0, \"cvss3_score\": \"4.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 4.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 4.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\", \"CWE-285\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 07 Oct 2021 17:07:22 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Thu, 27 Aug 2020 22:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"github.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"github.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.452+b00c5acad3\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10518\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10518\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.682, \"epss.score\": 0.00288}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A remote code execution vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that could be exploited when building a GitHub Pages site. User-controlled configuration of the underlying parsers used by GitHub Pages were not sufficiently restricted and made it possible to execute commands on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. To exploit this vulnerability, an attacker would need permission to create and build a GitHub Pages site on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. This vulnerability affected all versions of GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 2.22 and was fixed in 2.21.6, 2.20.15, and 2.19.21. The underlying issues contributing to this vulnerability were identified both internally and through the GitHub Security Bug Bounty program.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10518\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\", \"CWE-77\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Mon, 20 Dec 2021 22:35:23 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Thu, 27 Aug 2020 22:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"github.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"github.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A remote code execution vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that could be exploited when building a GitHub Pages site. User-controlled configuration of the underlying parsers used by GitHub Pages were not sufficiently restricted and made it possible to execute commands on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. To exploit this vulnerability, an attacker would need permission to create and build a GitHub Pages site on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. This vulnerability affected all versions of GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 2.22 and was fixed in 2.21.6, 2.20.15, and 2.19.21. The underlying issues contributing to this vulnerability were identified both internally and through the GitHub Security Bug Bounty program.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10518\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\", \"CWE-77\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Mon, 20 Dec 2021 22:35:23 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Thu, 27 Aug 2020 22:15:09 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"github.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"github.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.452+b00c5acad3\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10519\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10519\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.79899, \"epss.score\": 0.00708}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A remote code execution vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that could be exploited when building a GitHub Pages site. User-controlled configuration of the underlying parsers used by GitHub Pages were not sufficiently restricted and made it possible to execute commands on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. To exploit this vulnerability, an attacker would need permission to create and build a GitHub Pages site on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. This vulnerability affected all versions of GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 2.22.7 and was fixed in 2.22.7, 2.21.15, and 2.20.24. The underlying issues contributing to this vulnerability were identified through the GitHub Security Bug Bounty program.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10519\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\", \"CWE-77\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 07 Nov 2023 03:14:10 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 03 Mar 2021 04:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"github.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"github.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A remote code execution vulnerability was identified in GitHub Enterprise Server that could be exploited when building a GitHub Pages site. User-controlled configuration of the underlying parsers used by GitHub Pages were not sufficiently restricted and made it possible to execute commands on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. To exploit this vulnerability, an attacker would need permission to create and build a GitHub Pages site on the GitHub Enterprise Server instance. This vulnerability affected all versions of GitHub Enterprise Server prior to 2.22.7 and was fixed in 2.22.7, 2.21.15, and 2.20.24. The underlying issues contributing to this vulnerability were identified through the GitHub Security Bug Bounty program.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-10519\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\", \"CWE-77\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 07 Nov 2023 03:14:10 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 03 Mar 2021 04:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"github.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"github.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.452+b00c5acad3\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-8927\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-8927\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.78104, \"epss.score\": 0.0061}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-8927\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Tue, 08 Mar 2022 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-8927\", \"msrc.title\": \"Brotli Library Buffer Overflow Vulnerability\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A buffer overflow exists in the Brotli library versions prior to 1.0.8 where an attacker controlling the input length of a \\\"one-shot\\\" decompression request to a script can trigger a crash, which happens when copying over chunks of data larger than 2 GiB. It is recommended to update your Brotli library to 1.0.8 or later. If one cannot update, we recommend to use the \\\"streaming\\\" API as opposed to the \\\"one-shot\\\" API, and impose chunk size limits.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2020-8927\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 6.5, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.4\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.4, \"cvss3_score\": \"6.5\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 6.5, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 6.5\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-120\", \"CWE-130\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 2.5, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 07 Nov 2023 03:26:47 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 15 Sep 2020 10:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"powershell\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"7.1.3.sha:.33ce13a0df94183fde13a07ddee0722a017a8d1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4007\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4007\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.05402, \"epss.score\": 0.00042}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent, versions 3.0.1 to 3.1.2.34, suffer from a local privilege escalation due to an uncontrolled DLL search path. Specifically, when Insight Agent versions 3.0.1 to 3.1.2.34 start, the Python interpreter attempts to load python3.dll at \\\"C:\\\\DLLs\\\\python3.dll,\\\" which normally is writable by locally authenticated users. Because of this, a malicious local user could use Insight Agent\u0027s startup conditions to elevate to SYSTEM privileges. This issue was fixed in Rapid7 Insight Agent 3.1.2.35. This vulnerability is a regression of CVE-2019-5629.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4007\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"7.2\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 7.2, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-427\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 21 Dec 2021 14:52:22 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 14 Dec 2021 15:15:07 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4016\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4016\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.10424, \"epss.score\": 0.00044}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent, versions prior to 3.1.3, suffer from an improper access control vulnerability whereby, the user has access to the snapshot directory. An attacker can access, read and copy any of the files in this directory e.g. asset_info.json or file_info.json, leading to a loss of confidentiality. This issue was fixed in Rapid7 Insight Agent 3.1.3.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-4016\", \"cve_severity\": \"LOW\", \"cvss\": 3.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"2.1\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 2.1, \"cvss3_score\": \"3.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 3.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 3.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-Other\", \"CWE-284\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 1.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Fri, 05 Aug 2022 11:09:58 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 21 Jan 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-41355\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-41355\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.64605, \"epss.score\": 0.00255}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-41355\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Thu, 14 Oct 2021 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-41355\", \"msrc.title\": \".NET Core and Visual Studio Information Disclosure Vulnerability\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \".NET Core and Visual Studio Information Disclosure Vulnerability\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-41355\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 5.7, \"cvss2_score\": \"2.9\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 2.9, \"cvss3_score\": \"5.7\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 5.7, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 5.7\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.1, \"impact_score\": 3.6, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 01 Aug 2023 23:15:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 13 Oct 2021 01:15:13 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"powershell\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"7.1.3.sha:.33ce13a0df94183fde13a07ddee0722a017a8d1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"gui\", \"cisa_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-44228\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis_nvd\"], \"cve_description\": \"Apache Log4j2 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (excluding security releases 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and 2.3.1) JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker controlled LDAP and other JNDI related endpoints. An attacker who can control log messages or log message parameters can execute arbitrary code loaded from LDAP servers when message lookup substitution is enabled. From log4j 2.15.0, this behavior has been disabled by default. From version 2.16.0 (along with 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and 2.3.1), this functionality has been completely removed. Note that this vulnerability is specific to log4j-core and does not affect log4net, log4cxx, or other Apache Logging Services projects.\", \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-44228\", \"cve_severity\": \"CRITICAL\", \"cvss\": 10.0, \"cvss2_score\": \"9.3\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 9.3, \"cvss3_score\": \"10.0\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 10.0, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 10.0\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-20\", \"CWE-400\", \"CWE-502\", \"CWE-917\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 6.0, \"last_modified_date\": \"Tue, 07 Nov 2023 03:39:36 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 10 Dec 2021 10:15:09 GMT\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-44228\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-44228\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.99999, \"epss.score\": 0.97565}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-44228\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Thu, 16 Dec 2021 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2021-44228\", \"msrc.title\": \"Apache Log4j Remote Code Execution Vulnerability\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-0237\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-0237\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.05402, \"epss.score\": 0.00042}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Rapid7 Insight Agent versions 3.1.2.38 and earlier suffer from a privilege escalation vulnerability, whereby an attacker can hijack the flow of execution due to an unquoted argument to the runas.exe command used by the ir_agent.exe component, resulting in elevated rights and persistent access to the machine. This issue was fixed in Rapid7 Insight Agent version 3.1.3.80.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-0237\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"7.2\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 7.2, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-428\", \"CWE-264\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 24 Mar 2022 19:21:21 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Thu, 17 Mar 2022 23:15:07 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"rapid7 insight agent\", \"software_vendor\": \"rapid7, inc.\", \"software_version\": \"3.0.4.1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-24512\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-24512\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.75958, \"epss.score\": 0.00506}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-24512\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Fri, 14 Apr 2023 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-24512\", \"msrc.title\": \".NET and Visual Studio Remote Code Execution Vulnerability\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \".NET and Visual Studio Remote Code Execution Vulnerability\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-24512\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 6.3, \"cvss2_score\": \"6.8\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 6.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"6.3\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 6.3, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 6.3\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 3.4, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 21 Dec 2023 01:43:55 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 09 Mar 2022 17:15:15 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"powershell\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"7.1.3.sha:.33ce13a0df94183fde13a07ddee0722a017a8d1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26136\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26136\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.78872, \"epss.score\": 0.00651}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A vulnerability in multiple Atlassian products allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to bypass Servlet Filters used by first and third party apps. The impact depends on which filters are used by each app, and how the filters are used. This vulnerability can result in authentication bypass and cross-site scripting. Atlassian has released updates that fix the root cause of this vulnerability, but has not exhaustively enumerated all potential consequences of this vulnerability. Atlassian Bamboo versions are affected before 8.0.9, from 8.1.0 before 8.1.8, and from 8.2.0 before 8.2.4. Atlassian Bitbucket versions are affected before 7.6.16, from 7.7.0 before 7.17.8, from 7.18.0 before 7.19.5, from 7.20.0 before 7.20.2, from 7.21.0 before 7.21.2, and versions 8.0.0 and 8.1.0. Atlassian Confluence versions are affected before 7.4.17, from 7.5.0 before 7.13.7, from 7.14.0 before 7.14.3, from 7.15.0 before 7.15.2, from 7.16.0 before 7.16.4, from 7.17.0 before 7.17.4, and version 7.21.0. Atlassian Crowd versions are affected before 4.3.8, from 4.4.0 before 4.4.2, and version 5.0.0. Atlassian Fisheye and Crucible versions before 4.8.10 are affected. Atlassian Jira versions are affected before 8.13.22, from 8.14.0 before 8.20.10, and from 8.21.0 before 8.22.4. Atlassian Jira Service Management versions are affected before 4.13.22, from 4.14.0 before 4.20.10, and from 4.21.0 before 4.22.4.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26136\", \"cve_severity\": \"CRITICAL\", \"cvss\": 9.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"9.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 9.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 9.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-287\", \"CWE-180\"], \"exploitability_score\": 3.9, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:50:26 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 20 Jul 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26137\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26137\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.67503, \"epss.score\": 0.00277}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"A vulnerability in multiple Atlassian products allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to cause additional Servlet Filters to be invoked when the application processes requests or responses. Atlassian has confirmed and fixed the only known security issue associated with this vulnerability: Cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) bypass. Sending a specially crafted HTTP request can invoke the Servlet Filter used to respond to CORS requests, resulting in a CORS bypass. An attacker that can trick a user into requesting a malicious URL can access the vulnerable application with the victim\\u2019s permissions. Atlassian Bamboo versions are affected before 8.0.9, from 8.1.0 before 8.1.8, and from 8.2.0 before 8.2.4. Atlassian Bitbucket versions are affected before 7.6.16, from 7.7.0 before 7.17.8, from 7.18.0 before 7.19.5, from 7.20.0 before 7.20.2, from 7.21.0 before 7.21.2, and versions 8.0.0 and 8.1.0. Atlassian Confluence versions are affected before 7.4.17, from 7.5.0 before 7.13.7, from 7.14.0 before 7.14.3, from 7.15.0 before 7.15.2, from 7.16.0 before 7.16.4, from 7.17.0 before 7.17.4, and version 7.21.0. Atlassian Crowd versions are affected before 4.3.8, from 4.4.0 before 4.4.2, and version 5.0.0. Atlassian Fisheye and Crucible versions before 4.8.10 are affected. Atlassian Jira versions are affected before 8.13.22, from 8.14.0 before 8.20.10, and from 8.21.0 before 8.22.4. Atlassian Jira Service Management versions are affected before 4.13.22, from 4.14.0 before 4.20.10, and from 4.21.0 before 4.22.4.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26137\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-346\", \"CWE-180\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:45:16 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Wed, 20 Jul 2022 18:15:08 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_vendor\": \"atlassian.bitbucket.ui\", \"software_version\": \"2.0.394.beta+3fc6791abf\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26788\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26788\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.07513, \"epss.score\": 0.00043}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26788\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Tue, 10 May 2022 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26788\", \"msrc.title\": \"PowerShell Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"PowerShell Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2022-26788\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 7.8, \"cvss2_score\": \"4.6\", \"cvss2_score_num\": 4.6, \"cvss3_score\": \"7.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 7.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 7.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"NVD-CWE-noinfo\"], \"exploitability_score\": 1.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Thu, 29 Jun 2023 01:15:34 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Fri, 15 Apr 2022 19:15:12 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"powershell