bwebp 1.3.2 allowed a remote attacker to perform an out of bounds memory write via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Critical)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4863\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-787\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Sun, 07 Jan 2024 11:15:13 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 12 Sep 2023 15:15:24 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"google chrome\", \"software_vendor\": \"google inc.\", \"software_version\": \"104.0.5112.88\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Heap buffer overflow in libwebp in Google Chrome prior to 116.0.5845.187 and libwebp 1.3.2 allowed a remote attacker to perform an out of bounds memory write via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Critical)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4863\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-787\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Sun, 07 Jan 2024 11:15:13 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 12 Sep 2023 15:15:24 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"microsoft edge\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"101.0.1210.53\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Heap buffer overflow in libwebp in Google Chrome prior to 116.0.5845.187 and libwebp 1.3.2 allowed a remote attacker to perform an out of bounds memory write via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Critical)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4863\", \"cve_severity\": \"HIGH\", \"cvss\": 8.8, \"cvss3_score\": \"8.8\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 8.8, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 8.8\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-787\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.8, \"impact_score\": 5.9, \"last_modified_date\": \"Sun, 07 Jan 2024 11:15:13 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Tue, 12 Sep 2023 15:15:24 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"microsoft edge\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"103.0.1264.77\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-48795\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-48795\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.97981, \"epss.score\": 0.71637}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"The SSH transport protocol with certain OpenSSH extensions, found in OpenSSH before 9.6 and other products, allows remote attackers to bypass integrity checks such that some packets are omitted (from the extension negotiation message), and a client and server may consequently end up with a connection for which some security features have been downgraded or disabled, aka a Terrapin attack. This occurs because the SSH Binary Packet Protocol (BPP), implemented by these extensions, mishandles the handshake phase and mishandles use of sequence numbers. For example, there is an effective attack against SSH\u0027s use of ChaCha20-Poly1305 (and CBC with Encrypt-then-MAC). The bypass occurs in chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com and (if CBC is used) the -etm@openssh.com MAC algorithms. This also affects Maverick Synergy Java SSH API before 3.1.0-SNAPSHOT, Dropbear through 2022.83, Ssh before 5.1.1 in Erlang/OTP, PuTTY before 0.80, AsyncSSH before 2.14.2, golang.org/x/crypto before 0.17.0, libssh before 0.10.6, libssh2 through 1.11.0, Thorn Tech SFTP Gateway before 3.4.6, Tera Term before 5.1, Paramiko before 3.4.0, jsch before 0.2.15, SFTPGo before 2.5.6, Netgate pfSense Plus through 23.09.1, Netgate pfSense CE through 2.7.2, HPN-SSH through 18.2.0, ProFTPD before 1.3.8b (and before 1.3.9rc2), ORYX CycloneSSH before 2.3.4, NetSarang XShell 7 before Build 0144, CrushFTP before 10.6.0, ConnectBot SSH library before 2.2.22, Apache MINA sshd through 2.11.0, sshj through 0.37.0, TinySSH through 20230101, trilead-ssh2 6401, LANCOM LCOS and LANconfig, FileZilla before 3.66.4, Nova before 11.8, PKIX-SSH before 14.4, SecureCRT before 9.4.3, Transmit5 before 5.10.4, Win32-OpenSSH before 9.5.0.0p1-Beta, WinSCP before 6.2.2, Bitvise SSH Server before 9.32, Bitvise SSH Client before 9.33, KiTTY through 0.76.1.13, the net-ssh gem 7.2.0 for Ruby, the mscdex ssh2 module before 1.15.0 for Node.js, the thrussh library before 0.35.1 for Rust, and the Russh crate before 0.40.2 for Rust.\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-48795\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 5.9, \"cvss3_score\": \"5.9\", \"cvss3_score_num\": 5.9, \"cvss_str\": \"CVSS 5.9\", \"cvss_version\": \"v3.0\", \"cwe_id\": [\"CWE-354\"], \"exploitability_score\": 2.2, \"impact_score\": 3.6, \"last_modified_date\": \"Mon, 29 Jan 2024 09:15:42 GMT\", \"publish_date\": \"Mon, 18 Dec 2023 16:15:10 GMT\", \"software_name\": \"powershell\", \"software_vendor\": \"microsoft corporation\", \"software_version\": \"7.1.3.sha:.33ce13a0df94183fde13a07ddee0722a017a8d1\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"epss_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4901\", \"epss.creation_date\": \"Tue, 05 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT\", \"epss.cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4901\", \"epss.percentile\": 0.46963, \"epss.score\": 0.0013}, {\"adapters\": [\"msrc_enrichment\"], \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4901\", \"msrc.creation_date\": \"Fri, 15 Sep 2023 00:00:00 GMT\", \"msrc.cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4901\", \"msrc.title\": \"Chromium: CVE-2023-4901 Inappropriate implementation in Prompts\"}, {\"adapters\": [\"static_analysis\"], \"cve_description\": \"Inappropriate implementation in Prompts in Google Chrome prior to 117.0.5938.62 allowed a remote attacker to potentially spoof security UI via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Medium)\", \"cve_from_sw_analysis\": true, \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2023-4901\", \"cve_severity\": \"MEDIUM\", \"cvss\": 4.3